The game saves bones files for the mines but not for Sokoban. 
Implementing bones files for Sokoban is not going to be all that
different from implementing bones files for the mines.  I wonder why
that decision was made.

I die a lot more in the mines than I do in Sokoban.  That makes Sokoban
bones less valuable.

With Sokoban a bones file can contain plenty of destroyed boulders.  The
chance isn't high that both boulders and the scolls of earth are
destroyed, but if that happens the branch might become "not winable"
(the branch not the game).  I have yet to see any mine bones file that
stopped the mines brand from being "winable" (the branch not the game).
That makes Sokoban bones more risky in a way not correlated with the
dangers of bones files.

In Sokoban a bones file can keep you from finding our which of the
prizes was generated.  That's my guess why it was not implemented by the
DevTeam.  I think they decided that even though the game can be won
haivng skipped both of these two branches, they wanted to make sure each
branch was at least in principle winnable.

I don't think implemeting soko-bones would be a problem, but I do get
why it was not implemented.  if it gets implemented in some branch that
does not keep save files intact release to release it would be a nice
change.  I probably would not bother loading a patch that breaks save
files to add it to vanilla.


